## §3 — Transcript

```go
type Transcript struct { /* hidden */ }
func (t *Transcript) Append(msgs ...Message) (Position, error)
func (t *Transcript) Slice(from, to Position) []Message          // snapshot, non-blocking
func (t *Transcript) Subscribe(cursor Position) (<-chan Message, func())  // real-time bridge
type Position int64
```

- **Flat, not tree** (design note). Transcript is a linear append-only log. Fork/branch/undo/time-travel are product-layer concerns — build a tree view on top, not inside core. Pi's `LeafEntry` is the product-layer reference.
- **No internal mirror** (C6). Loop reads from `Transcript.Slice`, never from a cached copy.
- **`Subscribe`** bridges to TUI/WebSocket consumers (see `05-access-points.md`). Loop is decoupled.

